<TeXmacs|2.1.5>

<style|<tuple|tmdoc|english>>

<\body>
  <tmdoc-title|Short description of the <name|JavaScript> plug-in>

  In the version of <TeXmacs> which runs in a web browser, <name|JavaScript>
  sessions and executable folds run the <name|JavaScript> of the page
  itself: the interpreter of the browser which runs <TeXmacs>. They show
  what happens in the page, change it, and drive <TeXmacs> from
  <name|JavaScript>, as <name|Scheme> sessions do from <name|Scheme>. The
  plug-in exists only in a browser.

